Winter barley, on the other hand, produces 6.3 per cent more.
Harvesting will also grow rye.
Cypriot harvesters are estimated at 1.305 million tons, compared to last year more.
Settlements expanded by 7.3 per cent.
Hectare yield will be 3.2 percent lower than last year.
This year's rapeseed crops will outperute the ten-year average by 13.3 per cent, sown on an area a third more extensive than ten years ago.
In the last four years, the poppy fields have also been increasing.
Farmers planted 35,543 hectares this year.
Compared to 2008, when poppies in the Czech Republic were cultivated on a record of 70 000 hectares, however, there are half of the poppies.
Thanks to the expansion of sowing surfaces, this year's poppy harvest will be richer.
Compared to last year, it will rise by 2.5 percent to 27,423 tons.
Hectare yield will be 6.1 per cent lower.
