It eased when it almost disappeared eight years ago and had to be redeemed from the debt.
At the same time, strategic brands used "RBS" in order to protect other brands of consumer finance.
There were millions of pounds spent on the sponsorship of international sport, ranging from rugby Six Nations to Winbledom champion Andy Marray.
But now it has been decided that it is better to give more stand out for national brands.
The Royal Bank of Scotland will be used by Scottish customers, but it will not launch new stores.
All RBS references in England and Wales, with the exception of the headquarters and coordinating shares on the stock exchange, will be changed to NatWest.
The Ulster Bank brand is already used for customers in the Republic of Ireland and Northern Ireland.
There are other, smaller private-banking brands that will come to the forefront - Coutts, Adam & Co, Drummond, and Holt's Military Bank.
