Half the funeral services don’t comply with the rules.
Half of funeral service providers don't comply with the law.
The Czech Trade Inspection Authority (ČOI) discovered this during inspections in the second quarter.
Funeral services most often do not inform the bereaved of their prices or do not issue a written confirmation of the receipt of the order.
For this, the CTIA imposed 41 fines totalling 73,000 crowns.
Its spokeswoman Jiří Fröhlich informed about this today.
The inspectors found misconceptions at 47 out of 95 inspections.
Apart from non-adjudication of prices and missing receipts, some burial services also sold products or provided services at prices other than those agreed.
In five cases the products sold were not properly labelled and once the seller used an officially unverified gauge.
The inspection therefore banned the sale of 23 products for a total of CZK 7077.
It concerned urn wrappers, candle covers and vases that weren't properly labeled with obligatory information.
"Given that there is still a violation of the law in this specific area of services, the control action will continue in the next quarter of this year," Fröhlich added.
The London schoolgirl who joined IS was Killed in Syria
Kadida Sultana, one of the three British schoolgirls who left London last year to join IS, has died in Syria.
Lawyer Tasnime Akunjee said the family learned of her death in Raqqa, Syria, a few weeks ago.
ITV News announced on Thursday that it was believed to have been killed during a Russian airstrike in Raqqqa, a group's stronghold.
Sultana was 17 years old, and according to her family, she died just as she was preparing to flee from a war-torn country and a return to Britain.
"One wants to be believed to believe that the only good in the whole thing - as a message and a warning for others, that these are the real dangers associated with the way into the war zone - is that it will discourage people from ever making a decision," Akunjee said.
Sultan and two other schoolgirls from the eastern part of London boarded a plane in February 2015 on Turkey and then on a bus to the Syria border.
Sultana's family has learned that she married an IS fighter in Syria - and within a few months she was widowed.
