They want to compete with carriers.
Television director Matěj Liška and Marek Greger, the manager of the Prague music club, are behind the idea of using already planned shipments.
With the idea, they inhaled a trio of applications with a different geographical reach.
We lowered the Domestic Pre-Bringing app in May.
Thousousands of cities are recorded in it at this time and we will expand the network.
In the Czech Republic we first want to learn this than we will focus more on foreign countries, the forty-two-year-old manager says in an interview for iDNES.cz.
How does the Takeover app work and who can benefit from it?
You will download it and you will register for free.
Then you can enter the route and data on how much you can transfer the package and how much you want for it.
On that day, someone is asking for a transfer.
When it suits the route as well as the time of delivery, it is paired, and a mutual notification will come for both of them.
At that moment, the chat opens, where the couple arranges a handover.
In your opinion, how many people would rather have to register so that each package should always find their courier?
I don’t know the ideal situation, I can’t estimate how many registered and how many ways it is needed in order for the coverage to be quite optimal, and each supply is paired with demand.
It already works on the main roads and it's logically simpler than on the road between villages.
The more people, the greater the potential for speed and accuracy.
In the meantime, too, people are building their trust and find that no one will run away with the package.
So far you did not have to deal with such a case?
How many users does the service have after two months of launch?
At the moment we have about 5 to 6 thousand people who create paths.
We consider this as a success and we believe that there will be more.
Isn't there going to be a risk of waiting too long for the sender?
We hope that we will be a competitor for large conglomerates just because we are only able to deliver the matter the same day and for a fraction of the price.
You will pay a few thousand at a large company for delivery within two hours.
Here you will pay a Hundred or less, because this is a path that someone is already doing.
Should traditional carriers in the future be concerned about the possible loss of customers in the future?
We hope that's the way it is.
The market has a huge amount of potential, huge multi-strength carriers are feeding here, as well as retail chains, where everyone began to buy and gradually found out that the quality does not match what they were paying for.
No one wants to find in the inbox with a message that they have to pick up the shipment at the branch, at first that day after 19 o'clock.
At that time I already needed the package for six hours and I waited at home because it was important.
We want a better, quicker and functional service that won't annoy anyone and send a signal to the competitor to try.
Marek Greger (41) and Matěj Liška (39).
None of them ever worked in the field of information technology.
Marek Greger works as the manager of the music club, Matěj Liška as a television director.
In 2014 they began to prepare the Shippansee LTD application, which uses already planned trips between the world's metropolises to transport packages, especially by aircraft.
In 2015, they commissioned a project for the elaboration of a company that created applications such as MALL.cz, Jobs.cz or ČSFD.
The programming lasted three-quarters of a.m. year and launched the application in March 2016.
They began to develop the Převez application in December last year and released in May this year.
It is a local version of Shippansee adapted for the Czech market.
They have been developing the Mesík and Mesík Profi app since January this year and made it available to users at the end of July 2016.
The intent was from the very beginning to do all these applications, which will one day merge into one.
In the Czech Republic they want to fine-tune the application and then, in cooperation with a strong investor, focus more on the global market.
The sharing economy has recently been a theme, and this is an AirBnB or Uber service.
Aren't you worried about an action in an area that no one yet can say, where's the threshold of sharing and where the grey economy is?
It's the same, just a different product.
It is clear to us that if it is a success and we go up with it, we will be the next thorn in the eye through the grey economy.
But although someone saves and someone earns, it is not the intent to circumnate tax authorities and tax inspections.
Each user, on the one side or the other, will be urged to tax their income if they make an income.
From what do you think the service has so much potential?
The sender saves money and the transporter earns, respectively, reduces the cost of the journey.
Therein lies the strong idea that connects the interest on both sides.
In the age of social networks that divide people, we'd like this, on the contrary.
There may be nice stories, people are delighted that they have helped someone and will talk about it.
Maybe someone will bring you forgotten glasses, keys or pills.
In my opinion, people have been lacking a personal approach for a long period of time, about this app we say that it's a service of people to people.
So how do you guarantee that the courier does not fade with the package?
Each user of the application together with registration scans the identity card and indicates a bank connection, a payment or credit card.
These are canals that give service and a person a believable.
Coulters also collect asterisks based on sender ratings.
We will also offer insurance, the details are still fine-tuned.
The uninsured shipment in the event of loss or damage is guaranteed by the courier, but he does not take responsibility under the criminal law for the content, if there is something illegal inside and he does not know about it.
If he is stopped by the police and finds a submachine gun or ten kilos of hashish in a closed package in his suitcase, he will ancedairate criminal liability to the sender.
Is there a threat of miscarriable data from the database?
Responsible, if necessary, are traceable by the administrative body, which is the only one who will have the opportunity to look into it, even we ourselves are not able to see them, the data are protected against misuse.
How much money does the courier get after successful delivery of the shipment?
Courier determines the price and gets the full amount he asks for.
The sender is charged a few percent extra for mediation of contact.
This money is our profit, but it is only a few percent, because we want to put pressure on the volume.
The courier also cannot be accumulating that he did not deliver the shipment when he actually delivered it, the takeover and delivery is verified using QR codes.
Are there any restrictions?
In relation to the size or content of the package?
You can transport anything.
We've got three greats, little like a cube of butter, medium as a plato of eggs, and big as a bass of beers.
After that, there is no further restriction, and if someone has a place in the car, they will transport the refrigerator, for example.
The sender has an option to take a picture of the package in the app, so the courier can see what he wants.
You don’t even have to pack the matter if you don’t want to hide the content.
Shove the forgotten hoodie into the courier's hand and that's it.
Who came up with an idea and how long did it take to launch the service?
A friend got an idea more than two years ago, I didn’t pay a lot of attention at that time.
Then he showed me a demo application with a multi-sized range, which focuses mainly on air passengers.
That's when I told him I wouldn't be looking for an investor, but I'd want to stand by him and put savings into it.
The next year it took a development than we founded Shippanse LTD in London due to the increased creditworthiness of the entire product.
However, this isn't a version that you're first of all concentrivating on right now.
No, we focused marketing on the Czech Republic, where we try to catch the application, because it all had childbirth aches and there is still something to deal with and improve.
We are trying to respond to the feedback from customers and we do not deal with the foreign market so much at the moment.
We know it's a long-distance run, but we don't hurry, we want to create a really good product for people.
Shippansee LTD was a basic and most expensive application, the other two were in a way upgraded.
It was created when we said that the national segment can be much more interesting and that we will at least learn it in the Czech Republic.
The third Mesík application is local, for the city.
However, it can send the package to the exact address at the other end of the world.
It works for the sender in the same way I take over, but the difference is that as a courier you can see shipments in the form of points on the map that are closest to you, thanks to the geolocator on your mobile.
Applications for couriers who want to make a living from it, we have called Messík Profi.
So can someone make money by picking up packages around the city?
Exactly, the last application will be downloaded in Prague by a taxi driver, a student, a mother on parental leave, someone who wants to make the trip to work.
As they're all fooling around right now, they can pick up exactly the same way.
One can see where there are orders around the city, come to it, click and see when it has to be delivered and transports the shipment.
It's cheaper than competing services.
At the moment, we are still creating a web interface, which will be pivotal for companies for sending shipments, on the site they will fill in the data about them, i.e. they will create points on the map.
Then we are capable of invoicing their services every month.
Do you now pursue a full-time project?
It exploits us, but we normally have it at our job so that we can support and develop the project.
There is not a strong multinational investor behind us, we are two boys, one of whom had an ingenious idea, and the other jumped into it with other suggestions and ideas.
Now we are looking for an investor strong enough to be able to compete with us not the Czech market, but who should go to the global product with us and become another huge player in the market such as AirBnB and Uber.
Titanfall 2 is supposed to bring an all-forgotten variety.
It will correct the second installment and the solo game will be more varied according to the first information than in Call of Duty.
The length will be around the standard eight hours and the filling is to be based precisely on the concept of the merchandise in the first part.
Therefore, you can look forward to freedom of movement, which, in addition to running, also includes the possibility of using a combat titan.
In Addition to action arrogant passages, the game will contain levels aimed at skilful movement.
They're going to be reminiscent of platformers and include puzzles.
For example, double jumps, running on the walls and a rope glide are essential to overwhelmilate them.
In addition, it will sometimes be necessary to liquidate even enemies.
There will also be maps commemorating mazes and levels with special concepts.
In one, for example, it will be possible to lift and descend the platforms and close massive doors.
Thus, you will adjust the form of a battlefield.
Thanks to this, the pace of the game should oscillate between ferocious action and calmer moments to explore an unfamiliar planet.
We're going to play for Jack Cooper's pawn, dreaming of a pilot's career.
At the beginning of the campaign, along with Captain Lastimos, the Cooper crashes on the extraterrestrial planet Typhon inhabited by hostile soldiers.
There will also be no wilderness to him.
In addition, Lastimosa suffers deadly shots in the crash, and Cooper is therefore tasked to put the captain's titan.
Thus, his prognosis for the pilot's career will come true sooner than he had expected.
However, the first step will be to steal the battery necessary for the robot's repair.
Cooper's conversations with titan will also be significant.
Players will serve as a source of information about the soldier's past, at the same time, humorous moments will be created by robot depersonalized communication.
For example, if titanium is dryly listing all the injuries to Cooper at the planned spear.
First information about the campaign in Titanfall 2 was provided by the server Polygon.
In addition, it will be possible to assess the result already in two months and Bonusweb after Gamescom will bring you the first impressions of the network game.
Titanfall 2 launches on October 28 for PC, PlayStation 4 and Xbox One.
The THQ brand will come to life, but the original publishing house remains dead.
The Swedish company Nordic changes its name to THQ Nordic.
After the collapse of the THQ publishing house in 2013, it acquired a number of its brands and the right to use the logo and the name of the company.
Thanks to this, Nordic has been released by Darksiders 2 Deathnitive Edition and Red Faction Collection.
In addition, there are another 23 games for the publishing house, and 13 of them have not yet been uncovered by the company.
Thirty years ago, when I was retiring, my wife, after thirty years of marriage, found a twenty-year-old man, our neighbor.
I've known it from the very beginning - at first she's obviously been tempted for a long period of time, then they got together.
He's such a big guy, probably her type, because she used to walk in front of me like that.
She's completely gone crazy.
In those first days she even changed her voice, she had such a maiden, in love.
But when I told her I knew what's going on, she deniebrated it.
I've been observing it.
At that time he came from work regularly at six-thirty, so she always went shopping at the age of three.
Every day she tried to at least see him.
Later I found out that they were coming together in his house, in the laundry room.
How many times I've ever known they'd just been there.
I got the keys, decided to catch them there.
But I don't know why, in the end I've always stayed at home.
I've never been able to go there, to take that decisive step.
You might be laughing at me, but I believe that my wife used to control me mentally.
I soon found out that I'd be manoeuvrable to do what she wanted.
And I actually did it.
Maybe I'm just such a slip.
At the same time, the neighbors told me that they also knew about it.
I was such a jerk I never asked them what to do.
I've been afraid that if it had all cracked, it's going to be bad.
That it would happen to everyone in the family, only the daughter knew something.
So I've always put it off, on and on.
But one day I went to see him in an apartment that I would need help with something in the laundry room.
He went there with me and I told him that I had received an Anonymous, that he was meeting with my wife, and that he was suggesting.
I asked him what he was going to tell me.
He stood there, shrugging his shoulders, staring at the ground, not saying a word.
At the same time I met his wife on the way out of the store.
I told her, but she couldn't believe it at all.
She didn’t react to it, and she didn’t tell me anything.
No one told me anything at the time.
I'm such a person who has never gone anywhere, who has a hard time acquainted with someone, let's find a feminine.
So I didn't even think about the divorce.
I've always relied on it coming to an end one day.
I thought I'm going to forsaken all of this, and life would go on.
It wasn't like that.
Basically, I've probably never come to terms with all of this.
To this day, I still have it in me.
Earlier I used to show it to her quite often, but in the end I left it for peace of mind.
He continues to live in the house next door, and I continue to live with her.
It's just my housewife rather than my housewife.
At home she always did everything - she cooked, washed, she was cleaning.
- She's industrious.
In my opinion, she has always struggled so I wouldn't have any other reason to complain.
You can say he's also good.
But sometimes I'd want to caress, hugs her, and she doesn't let go.
We're going for walks and shopping together, and we all think what a happy marriage we've got.
But she once told me that she never loved me.
That she had and liked me, but that she didn't love me.
And I can see that she still loves him to this day, he is her god.
I don’t enjoy such a life.
Even then, when it started and I carried it very badly, I once told her that I didn’t want to live and I asked me what she would say if it ended.
I wanted to know if she'd agree with it or not.
And that's what I wanted to hear from her: Yes or not.
