The symptoms occur an hour to two weeks after quen’ation of an undergradually processed infected fish.
After three weeks from the onslide of the larva disease, they usually spontaneously leave the indigestive tract.
Adult worms and larvae are susceptible to both higher and low temperatures, which is why they are killed either with sufficient heat treatment of fish meat or when it is frozen.
Veterinarians have currently also examined the salmon with the recipient of imported goods in the Central Bohemian Region.
