U.S.-U.S. Trade Rises 71% - RT Business
According to the Russian ambassador to Iran Levan Dzhagaryan, the trade turnover rose by 70.9 percent year-on-year after lifting sanctions between Moscow and Tehran.
As the ambassador said, there has been an increase in interest by Russian companies that do business in the country since international sanctions were lifted.
Russian companies rebuild existing ties with Iran, while the new firms are ready to enter the market.
A further expansion of commerce is, of course, one of the main priorities of bilateral cooperation with Iran," Dzhagaryan said.
Remarked that in the first five months of 2016, the trade turnover between Russia and Iran grew by 70.9 percent compared to the same period for 2015, reaching $856 million.
Specifically, Russia's exports to Iran went 91.5 per cent, amounting to $6.97 million.
U.S. imports from Iran have risen 16 per cent to $158 million.
Leap growth in trade ensured the supply of machinery, ground vehicles and weapons," the ambassador said.
Dzhagaryan also expects Russia to visit a record number of tourists from Iran this year.
In the past year, the Russian diplomatic mission in Iran has handed down around 35,000 visas to the citizens of Iran.
In addition, for the first time, Iran is among the top 20 countries according to the number of hikers arriving in Russia.
It can safely be said that the record numbers of tourists from Iran in Russia last year will be surpassed," he said.
At the same time, however, Iran visits a relatively small number of Russians. The ambassador hopes that there will be a change.
"Personally, I can recommend a visit to Isfahan, Shiraz and Yazd, where there are in good condition the surviving monuments of an ancient Persian civilization," he said.
