The names Pat and Mat then got DIYers in 1985, this time it was filmed directly for the short film Prague.
In 1990 Lubomír Beneš founded his own studio of the animated film AIF Studio in Prague and Zurich, where other parts were created.
After his death in 1995, other works with other creators continued, many of whom Beneš's son Marek participated.
At present, there are over ninety-eight episodes with the stories of these do-it-chilleries, who pour everything under their hands, but they are never angry at each other and are always full of optimism, ideas and DIY enthusiasm, and in the end they are satisfied with their work, which will be documented by a well-familiar gesture "... and that's it!".
